  "bio": "The \"Digital Media program\" offered by the Faculty of Modern Media is based on a new curriculum in an ever-renewing technological media field, enabling students to acquire theoretical… 133 CH — Univ. Req. 14 · Univ. Elec. 8 · Colg. Req. 42 · Spec. Req. 33 · Spec. Elec. 9 · Free Elec. 6 · Support 21. Semester order is a suggested prerequisite-valid sequence — no official one was published. Courses, hours and prerequisites are as published.",
  "bioAr": null,
  "overview": "The \"Digital Media program\" offered by the Faculty of Modern Media is based on a new curriculum in an ever-renewing technological media field, enabling students to acquire theoretical knowledge and practical skills to become journalists engaged in an ever-renewing digital environment. This is by making the teaching structure based on field work, providing an educational environment enhanced by laboratories dedicated to experimentation and presenting media content, and communicating with a team of academics and specialized experts.This program also focuses on everything that would provide the student with skills that would enable him/her to work independently, capable of creating media content, by enabling them to produce by themselves and create entrepreneurial pioneering projects in a world that is no longer the exclusive to large institutions.This program provides four educational fields that bring the students closer to the labor market in the field they prefer and find themselves in, so that they can choose the field of modern media technologies, digital journalism, digital photography, or digital radio and televisionOverviewThe \"Digital Media program\" offered by the Faculty of Modern Media is based on a new curriculum in an ever-renewing technological media field, enabling students to acquire theoretical knowledge and practical skills to become journalists engaged in an ever-renewing digital environment. This is by making the teaching structure based on field work, providing an educational environment enhanced by laboratories dedicated to experimentation and presenting media content, and communicating with a team of academics and specialized experts.This program also focuses on everything that would provide the student with skills that would enable him/her to work independently, capable of creating media content, by enabling them to produce by themselves and create entrepreneurial pioneering projects in a world that is no longer the exclusive to large institutions.This program provides four educational fields that bring the students closer to the labor market in the field they prefer and find themselves in, so that they can choose the field of modern media technologies, digital journalism, digital photography, or digital radio and television",
